# The repo's ONE env file. Copy it to .env here at the repo root (gitignored) and fill in what you have.
# NEVER put a real value in .env.example: CI's secrets guard blocks the PR, and a pushed key must be rotated.
#
# The game page needs no keys. The Kiro server (docs/PRD.md SYS-12, game/server/README.md) runs `kiro-cli acp` (D-04, D-190):
#   - with KIRO_API_KEY set, the key is passed to kiro-cli's environment;
#   - with it empty, kiro-cli uses its own login on this machine (`kiro-cli login`), which is how the team runs it.
# With neither, every Kiro feature falls back to rule-written text, labelled "Kiro (offline)" (KIRO-09).
# On Fly.io (docs/HOSTING.md, D-200) this file is not used at all: the key is `fly secrets set KIRO_API_KEY=…`
# (an environment variable on the machine) and the Docker build never sees .env (.dockerignore).

KIRO_API_KEY=

# Optional: where the Kiro server listens (defaults 127.0.0.1:8787) and which binary it runs (default `kiro-cli`).
# PORT=8787
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# KIRO_CLI=kiro-cli
# Optional: where the Kiro server keeps its counters between restarts (default game/server/.state/runs.json; /data/runs.json in the Fly image).
# KIRO_STATE_FILE=
